282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 208 0 R
/E (To develop a graph-based urban traffic simulation and optimization system that models road networks using vertices and edges, utilizes real-world road data from OpenStreetMap, and estimates travel times using the Bureau of Public Roads \(BPR\) congestion function. The system aims to simulate traffic assignment, analyse congestion, investigate the Braess Paradox, and evaluate road network modifications such as converting roads to one-ways or widening roads and changing road capacities. By applying suitable graph algorithms and comparing metrics such as average travel time, congestion levels, and traffic throughput before and after interventions, UrbanFlow seeks to identify effective infrastructure changes that improve overall traffic flow and network efficiency.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
