<<
/Title (The Braess Paradox is a known result in transportation theory: adding or keeping open a road can raise total travel time. It happens because each driver picks the route that looks fastest to them, which is called User Equilibrium. In UrbanFlow's scenario, three roads connect an origin to a destination, and closing the quick middle road makes the whole network faster.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1746 0 R
/First 1763 0 R
/Last 1763 0 R
/Count -1
>>
